-- CONTROL 2/3 for s6-c1-rigid-goal-no-minimum: the SAME program with the user
-- impl DELETED.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER (hand-derived, NOT captured): match(IE, `Index (List (List a)) Int
-- (List a)`) is now the SINGLETON {prelude `impl Index (List b) Int b`}, which is
-- trivially its own ⊑-minimum. §6 C1 is satisfied, `inst` commits, and the program
-- prints element 0 of `[[1, 2], [3]]` -- `[1, 2]`.
--
-- WHY THIS CONTROL EXISTS: it pins that the rigid goal is well-formed and RESOLVES
-- on its own. Without it, the sibling's reject could be read as "a rigid goal
-- cannot be resolved at all" rather than "this rigid goal has no ⊑-minimum" -- and
-- the fix for those two readings is not the same fix. It is also the exact value
-- the buggy sibling printed before #1155, which is what made that bug invisible.
firstRow : List (List a) -> List a
firstRow xss = index xss 0

main = println (firstRow [[1, 2], [3]])
